    {
        "name": "Gastric Torsion",
        "name_ja": "胃捻転",
        "symptoms": {"bloating", "lethargy", "sudden_death"},
        "description": "Gastric Torsion is a clinical condition requiring veterinary evaluation, diagnosis, and appropriate treatment.",
        "description_ja": "過食や大きすぎる餌による胃捻転。",
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "recommended_tests": ["radiography", "clinical_examination"],
        "causes": "Caused by gastric torsion (volvulus) following ingestion of excessively large prey or overfeeding, resulting in rotation and obstruction of the stomach.",

        "causes_ja": "両生類における胃捻転の原因: 過食や大きすぎる餌による胃捻転。",
        "pathophysiology": "The pathological process involves tissue injury, inflammatory response, and progressive functional impairment. Without intervention, compensatory mechanisms may be overwhelmed, leading to clinical deterioration.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "胃捻転は両生類における消化器疾患である。粘膜の完全性、運動性、分泌機能、またはマイクロバイオームバランスの障害を伴う。炎症により上皮バリアが損傷し、吸収不良、体液喪失、細菌トランスロケーションの可能性がある。運動障害（低運動性/うっ滞または亢進）により通過時間と消化効率が変化する。後腸発酵動物では盲腸/結腸フローラの破壊が致死的ディスバイオーシスと腸管毒素症を引き起こしうる。",
        "treatment": "TRUE EMERGENCY - rapid intervention required. Stabilization (FIRST PRIORITY): Amphibian Ringer's solution (NaCl 6.6 g + KCl 0.15 g + CaCl₂ 0.15 g + NaHCO₃ 0.2 g per L) 25-50 mL/kg ICe q12h; warm to lower POTZ (reduces metabolic demand); handle minimally; place on moist paper towel in covered container. Analgesia: butorphanol 0.4-1 mg/kg SC/IM (preferred over opioids with respiratory depression) OR buprenorphine 38 mg/kg SC (amphibian-specific high dose, Stevens 2011); meloxicam 0.2 mg/kg IM/SC q48h (use cautiously - amphibian NSAID sensitivity). Anesthesia for intervention: MS-222 (tricaine methanesulfonate) 150-200 mg/L buffered to pH 7.0-7.4 with sodium bicarbonate - induction 5-10 min, maintain by misting gills/skin; monitor heart rate via Doppler/ECG. Gastric decompression: orogastric tube passage with Cole or red rubber catheter (lubricated with water-based gel, NOT petroleum) - gently advance to stomach, decompress gas/fluid; AVOID trocarization in amphibians (skin too delicate, high infection risk). Surgical correction (if torsion confirmed on radiographs/ultrasound): Ventral midline coeliotomy under MS-222 maintenance; assess gastric viability (pink = viable, black/green = necrotic); derotate stomach to normal anatomical position; gastropexy with 5-0 or 6-0 PDS to ventral body wall (prevents recurrence); resect any necrotic tissue with primary anastomosis using 6-0 monofilament. Peri-operative antibiotics: ceftazidime 20 mg/kg ICe/IM q72h × 10-14 days (Wright 2006) - PREFERRED first-line for amphibian surgical prophylaxis/treatment; alternative enrofloxacin 5-10 mg/kg IM/SC q24h (NOT for larvae - cartilage toxicity); amikacin 5 mg/kg ICe q48h only if hydrated (nephrotoxic). Post-operative: NPO 48-72 hours, then liquid nutritional support via gavage (Oxbow Critical Care Herbivore or Emeraid Omnivore 1-2 mL ICe/PO); monitor for reperfusion injury, cardiac arrhythmias (Doppler); warm humid recovery enclosure 100% humidity, POTZ mid-range; gradual reintroduction to normal feeding over 7-10 days with smaller prey items (<30% head width). Reference: Wright & Whitaker (2001) Amphibian Medicine and Captive Husbandry Ch 17.",
        "treatment_ja": "両生類胃捻転の治療: 真の緊急事態 - 迅速介入必須。【安定化（最優先）】両生類リンゲル液（NaCl 6.6g+KCl 0.15g+CaCl₂ 0.15g+NaHCO₃ 0.2g/L）25-50 mL/kg ICe q12h; POTZ下限に加温（代謝需要低下）; 最小限の取扱; 覆い付き容器内湿潤ペーパータオルに載せる。【鎮痛】ブトルファノール0.4-1 mg/kg SC/IM（呼吸抑制のあるオピオイドより優先）またはブプレノルフィン38 mg/kg SC（両生類特異的高用量、Stevens 2011）; メロキシカム0.2 mg/kg IM/SC q48h（両生類NSAID感受性のため慎重）。【介入用麻酔】MS-222（トリカイン）150-200 mg/L、重炭酸ナトリウムでpH 7.0-7.4緩衝 - 導入5-10分、鰓/皮膚ミスティングで維持; ドプラ/ECGで心拍監視。【胃減圧】Cole/赤ゴムカテーテルで経口胃管挿入（水性ゲル潤滑、石油系禁）- 胃まで慎重に前進、ガス/液体減圧; 両生類ではトロカール禁忌（皮膚脆弱、感染リスク高）。【外科的整復（レ線/超音波で捻転確認時）】MS-222維持下で腹正中切開; 胃生存性評価（ピンク=生存、黒/緑=壊死）; 正常解剖位置に整復; 5-0/6-0 PDSで腹壁に胃固定術（再発予防）; 壊死組織切除+6-0モノフィラメントで一次吻合。【周術期抗菌薬】セフタジジム20 mg/kg ICe/IM q72h × 10-14日（Wright 2006）- 両生類外科予防/治療の第一選択; 代替エンロフロキサシン5-10 mg/kg IM/SC q24h（幼生禁-軟骨毒性）; アミカシン5 mg/kg ICe q48h（水和時のみ、腎毒性）。【術後】48-72時間NPO、その後液体栄養をガベージ投与（Oxbow Critical Care HerbivoreまたはEmeraid Omnivore 1-2 mL ICe/PO）; 再灌流障害・心不整脈監視（ドプラ）; 湿度100%温暖回復環境、POTZ中央値; 7-10日かけて小型餌（<頭幅30%）で正常給餌復帰。文献: Wright & Whitaker (2001) Amphibian Medicine and Captive Husbandry 第17章。",
        "prevention": "Prevention focuses on appropriate prey sizing (prey item <30% of amphibian head width), avoiding overfeeding (feed to satiation 2-3 times weekly for adults rather than daily), ensuring proper POTZ for efficient digestion (species-specific temperature gradient), providing adequate enclosure space for normal movement patterns, avoiding handling/stress within 24 hours post-feeding, maintaining substrate that prevents accidental ingestion of oversized items.",
        "prevention_ja": "胃捻転の予防: 適切な餌サイズ（両生類頭幅の30%未満）、過食回避（成体は毎日より週2-3回満腹給餌）、効率的消化のための適切なPOTZ（種別温度勾配）、正常な運動パターンのための十分な飼育スペース、給餌後24時間以内の取扱/ストレス回避、過大物の誤食を防ぐ基質管理。",
        "prognosis": "Guarded to grave even with aggressive intervention. Early recognition (<6 hours from onset) with viable gastric tissue carries 40-60% survival with surgical correction. Delayed presentation (>12 hours) with gastric necrosis carries 10-20% survival. Key prognostic indicators: duration of torsion, gastric tissue viability at surgery, concurrent septic shock, species-specific resilience (toads generally more tolerant than frogs). Mortality often from septic shock or cardiac arrhythmias during reperfusion.",
        "prognosis_ja": "胃捻転の予後: 積極的介入でも慎重〜重篤。早期認識（発症<6時間）で胃組織生存例は外科的整復で生存率40-60%。遅延例（>12時間）で胃壊死は生存率10-20%。主要予後指標: 捻転持続時間、手術時胃組織生存性、併発敗血症性ショック、種別耐性（ヒキガエルはカエル類より概して耐容良好）。死亡原因は再灌流期敗血症性ショック・心不整脈が多い。",
        "onset_pattern": {"acute"},
        "age_predisposition": {"young", "adult", "senior"},
    },
    {
        "name": "Reproductive Failure / Egg Retention",
        "name_ja": "繁殖障害・卵停滞",
        "symptoms": {"bloating", "anorexia", "lethargy", "straining"},
        "description": "Reproductive Failure / Egg Retention in amphibians represents inability to oviposit due to environmental, hormonal, or physical factors.",
        "description_ja": "産卵障害による卵停滞と体腔炎。",
        "urgency": "high",
        "recommended_tests": ["ultrasound", "radiography", "blood_chemistry"],
        "causes": "Caused by: 1) Environmental: inadequate water temperature cycling, lack of breeding rain/water level changes, absence of appropriate substrate for egg-laying, low humidity/desiccation; 2) Hormonal: inadequate GnRH signaling, absence of male pheromone/courtship stimulation, poor body condition (malnutrition, obesity); 3) Physical: mechanical obstruction (pelvic abnormalities, oversized eggs), oviductal stricture/impaction, hypocalcemia-related neuromuscular failure; 4) Systemic disease: chronic illness, obesity, metabolic disorder.",

        "causes_ja": "両生類における繁殖障害・卵停滞の原因：環境因子（水温サイクル不適切、繁殖雨/水位変化不足、産卵基質不足、低湿度/乾燥）。ホルモン異常（GnRH不足、雄フェロモン/求愛刺激不足、不良な体況）。物理的閉塞（骨盤異常、過大卵、卵管狭窄/便秘、低カルシウム血症）。全身疾患（慢性疾患、肥満、代謝異常）。",
        "pathophysiology": "Egg retention in amphibians results from failed ovulation/oviposition due to inadequate HPO axis signaling or mechanical obstruction. Unlike terrestrial reptiles, amphibians require specific water triggers (rain, water level changes, temperature cycling) for breeding. Without these environmental cues, ovulation cascade does not initiate. If eggs develop (ovulation occurs) but oviposition fails, retained eggs accumulate within oviducts/coelomic cavity. Prolonged retention causes eggshell thinning/weakening, oviductal edema, vascular compromise, and bacterial translocation. Broken eggs leak yolk into coelomic cavity causing yolk coelomitis, peritonitis, and sepsis. In amphibians, thin/permeable skin permits rapid disease progression and sepsis.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "両生類の卵停滞は不十分なHPO軸刺激または機械的閉塞による排卵/産卵失敗で生じる。爬虫類と異なり両生類は繁殖に特定の水トリガー（雨、水位変化、温度サイクル）を必要。環境キューなしで排卵カスケード開始されず。卵発生（排卵成功）でも産卵失敗時、卵が卵管/体腔に蓄積。長期停滞で卵殻菲薄化/脆弱化、卵管浮腫、血管障害、細菌易位。両生類の薄い/透過性皮膚で疾患進行・敗血症が急速。",
        "treatment": "Environmental management (FIRST-LINE): Increase water temperature cycling (species-specific: temperate frogs 4-10°C winter/summer difference), provide simulated breeding rain (spray misting system, water level fluctuation), increase humidity to 100% (dense vegetation/sphagnum moss/high water access), simulate breeding season photoperiod/temperature. Medical intervention (if viable eggs present): Oxytocin 1-5 IU/kg IM (low amphibian tolerance to oxytocin). hCG 100-500 IU/kg IM as alternative. GnRH agonist (leuprolide 0.05-0.1 mg/kg IM × 1-2 doses). Supportive care: IV hydration (Ringer's lactate 50-100 mL/kg/day, but via intraperitoneal/intracoelomic route in amphibians; IV access difficult), calcium gluconate if hypocalcemic (50-100 mg/kg IV/IC), pain management (meloxicam 0.1-0.2 mg/kg IM q48h—use lowest dose due to amphibian sensitivity). Surgical intervention (if medical fails or rupture/coelomitis present): Exploratory celiotomy under MS-222 anesthesia (20-40 mg/L immersion to deep anesthesia) or topical/infiltrated lidocaine. Remove broken eggs, perform peritoneal lavage with sterile saline, debride necrotic tissue. Ovariohysterectomy for recurrent/refractory cases. Antibiotics if coelomitis: enrofloxacin 2.5-5 mg/kg IM/IV q48h × 21 days. Post-operative: Humid environment (100% humidity maintained), minimal handling, nutritional support when appetite returns.",
        "treatment_ja": "両生類の繁殖障害・卵停滞治療：環境管理（第一選択線）：水温サイクル増加（種別：温帯カエル冬夏で4-10℃差）、繁殖雨シミュレート（スプレーミスティング、水位変動）、湿度100%（密生植生/泥炭藻類/高水アクセス）、繁殖季節光周期/温度シミュレート。医学的介入（生存卵が存在する場合）：オキシトシン1-5 IU/kg IM（両生類は低耐容）。hCG 100-500 IU/kg IM 代替。GnRHアゴニスト（リュープロレリン0.05-0.1 mg/kg IM × 1-2回）。支持療法：IV給液（Ringer's乳酸塩50-100 mL/kg/日、両生類では腹腔/体腔内経路；IV困難）、低カルシウム血症時グルコン酸カルシウム50-100 mg/kg IV/IC、鎮痛（メロキシカム0.1-0.2 mg/kg IM q48h）。外科的介入（医学的管理失敗または破裂/体腔炎）：MS-222麻酔（20-40 mg/L浸液で深麻酔）下で体腔探索。破裂卵除去、滅菌食塩水で洗浄、壊死組織デブリード。再発/難治例で卵巣卵管摘出。体腔炎時抗菌薬：エンロフロキサシン2.5-5 mg/kg IM/IV q48h × 21日。術後：湿潤環境（100%湿度維持）、最小限の取扱、食欲回復後栄養補給。",
        "prevention": "Prevention includes: appropriate species-specific breeding environment simulation (water temperature cycling 4-10°C, breeding rain systems, high humidity 95-100%, vegetation), balanced diet adequate in calcium (calcium-rich prey: dusted crickets/flies), regular body weight monitoring, avoidance of obesity, reproductive health monitoring via palpation/ultrasound annually in breeding-age females, prompt treatment of any illness that might suppress breeding.",
        "prevention_ja": "繁殖障害の予防：種別繁殖環境シミュレート（水温サイクル4-10℃、繁殖雨システム、湿度95-100%、植生）、カルシウム豊富な食事（カルシウム富有餌：フンコロガシ/ハエ粉装）、定期体重監視、肥満回避、繁殖年齢メスの年1回生殖器モニタリング（触診/超音波）、繁殖を抑制する病気の迅速治療。",
        "prognosis": "Prognosis excellent if environmental cues are corrected before oviductal/egg damage develops. With proper breeding environment simulation (temperature cycling + breeding rain + humidity), >80% of amphibians resume normal breeding cycles. Medical/surgical intervention (oxytocin, hCG) has lower success rate (30-50%) in amphibians compared to reptiles. Ovariohysterectomy resolves reproductive failure but prevents future breeding. If coelomitis/sepsis has developed, prognosis is guarded (30-50% mortality even with aggressive treatment).",
        "prognosis_ja": "繁殖障害の予後：環境キューが卵管/卵損傷前に是正されれば予後優秀。適切な繁殖環境シミュレート（温度サイクル＋繁殖雨＋湿度）で>80%両生類が正常繁殖サイクル回復。医学的/外科的介入（オキシトシン、hCG）は両生類で爬虫類より低成功率（30-50%）。卵巣卵管摘出は繁殖障害を解決するが今後繁殖不可。体腔炎/敗血症発症時は予後慎重（積極的治療でも死亡率30-50%）。",
        "onset_pattern": {"subacute", "chronic"},
        "age_predisposition": {"young", "adult", "senior"},
    },
